WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.920
Good to have you on Planetary and Daily, Episode 85 for June 10th, 2026.

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:11.460
Let's get into today's research and health developments. AI analysis of normal mammograms

00:00:11.460 --> 00:00:17.920
can flag elevated breast cancer risk up to a decade before diagnosis. Retrospective data show

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:23.820
rising AI scores up to 10 years before diagnosis in women who later developed cancer.

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:30.240
The pattern also appears in a separate prospective analysis covering a 3-5-year window.

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:35.480
The method uses routine mammogram images already collected in clinical care.

00:00:36.400 --> 00:00:39.520
Validation in larger cohorts is the next reported step.

00:00:40.320 --> 00:00:45.400
Now we turn from early detection tools to cellular mechanisms that may drive disease progression.

00:00:46.480 --> 00:00:51.880
Researchers identified an epigenetic regulator acting on microglial mitochondria.

00:00:52.520 --> 00:00:57.740
The pro-inflammatory state of microglia drives disease progression in experimental models.

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:03.160
Targeting this regulator could alter mitochondrial function inside these immune cells.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:10.060
The finding opens a potential route for therapy or prevention. Work remains at the pre-clinical stage.

00:01:10.940 --> 00:01:15.900
Ancestral sequence reconstruction revives ancient enzymes by inferring protein sequences

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:21.620
through backward tracing of evolutionary history. The method targets enzymes that may have

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:27.880
performed optimally millions of years ago. Researchers apply the technique when modern versions fall

00:01:27.880 --> 00:01:34.560
short for biotechnology needs. The approach reconstructs sequences computationally before laboratory

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:41.980
testing. No specific performance metrics appear in the post. Soft bioelectronics advance wearable

00:01:41.980 --> 00:01:48.240
and implantable sensors through work in way gauze lab at Caltech. The lab develops stretchable,

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:54.120
tissue integrated devices. The sensors enable continuous monitoring and adaptive therapy.

00:01:54.880 --> 00:02:00.780
Materials combine softness and adhesion for long-term body contact. The work targets diagnosis

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:06.600
and treatment across multiple conditions. No quantitative performance data are provided in the

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:14.020
summary. Augmented reality ultrasound generates real-time 3D views through a system created by MIT

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:21.360
researchers. The system renders live three-dimensional ultrasound images. The display overlays the

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:27.620
volumetric data onto the patient's body. The design aims to simplify interpretation during scanning

00:02:27.620 --> 00:02:33.700
procedures. No patient numbers or accuracy metrics are stated. Clinical testing steps are not

00:02:33.700 --> 00:02:39.400
described. While disease mechanisms continue to be mapped at the cellular level, another study

00:02:39.400 --> 00:02:46.020
examines how everyday physiology responds to extreme endurance efforts. A review examined effects

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:52.480
of marathon running on the heart. It documented release of cardiac troponin and NTPRO-BNP

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:58.240
after races. These elevations occur without established clinical significance in most runners.

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:03.500
The analysis draws on existing studies of endurance exercise physiology.

00:03:04.220 --> 00:03:09.860
Future work may clarify whether repeated biomarker spikes influence long-term cardiac structure.

00:03:10.780 --> 00:03:16.480
Theoretical models predict beta decay rates in neutron-rich nuclei through calculations developed

00:03:16.480 --> 00:03:23.200
by TU-Darmstadt researchers. The rates influence models of heavy element formation in the universe.

00:03:24.040 --> 00:03:29.880
Calculations were compared with available experimental data. Results appear in physical review

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:36.780
letters. Further measurements will test additional nuclei. From acute exercise responses, we shift to

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:42.520
a behavioral intervention that may protect cognition during medical treatment. Cancer patients

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:48.140
following a structured home program maintained better attention scores. The trial compared the

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:54.440
intervention against a placebo condition. Low dose ibuprofen produce smaller and less consistent

00:03:54.440 --> 00:04:02.220
cognitive benefits. Up to 80% of chemotherapy recipients experience chemo-brain. The exercise protocol

00:04:02.220 --> 00:04:08.960
required no clinic visits. Glucosamine use tied to faster cognitive decline appears in a large

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:14.600
observational study that linked the supplement to accelerated progression from mild impairment to

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:20.560
Alzheimer's. Users showed a reported 25% higher likelihood of developing dementia.

00:04:21.480 --> 00:04:27.540
Biological measurements provided possible mechanistic clues. The association does not establish

00:04:27.540 --> 00:04:34.700
causation. Replication in additional cohorts is needed. Asexual reproduction slowed early animal

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:40.140
evolution according to fossil evidence indicating Earth's first animals reproduced asexually.

00:04:40.860 --> 00:04:46.840
Low competition communities limited morphological change over long periods. Environmental

00:04:46.840 --> 00:04:53.480
pressures later favored sexual reproduction. Biodiversity and evolutionary rates increased sharply

00:04:53.480 --> 00:04:59.880
afterward. The study draws on paleontological records. Staying with interventions that support

00:04:59.880 --> 00:05:05.360
brain health, our next segment examines how breast milk composition aligns with newborn brain

00:05:05.360 --> 00:05:12.220
development across species. A multi-university study compared fatty acid profiles across mammals.

00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:18.980
Humans showed the strongest alignment with prefrontal cortex development. The composition varies

00:05:18.980 --> 00:05:25.500
systematically between species. Finding support efforts to engineer infant formulas closer to human

00:05:25.500 --> 00:05:32.020
milk. The breast milk fatty acid study reveals species-specific tailoring that aligns most closely

00:05:32.020 --> 00:05:38.400
with human prefrontal cortex needs. This compositional matching likely supports rapid postnatal

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:43.960
brain growth unique to our lineage. The work supplies concrete targets for formula development,

00:05:44.180 --> 00:05:49.980
rather than generic nutrient lists. Global commission targets brain health as economic driver

00:05:49.980 --> 00:05:55.580
through the brain health for economic resilience commission, which will define and measure cognitive

00:05:55.580 --> 00:06:02.200
capacity. It frames brain health as a foundation for economic resilience. The effort is trans

00:06:02.200 --> 00:06:07.620
disciplinary and international. Nature medicine announced the initiative in a recent comment.

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:14.600
Specific metrics and timelines are not yet detailed. From early life nutrition to built-in patterns

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:20.200
that shape everyday movement, we look next at a surprising directional bias in human walking.

00:06:21.080 --> 00:06:27.080
Researchers in Spain and Japan tested people walking in varied group sizes. The vast majority

00:06:27.080 --> 00:06:33.020
preferred counterclockwise turns, regardless of culture or gender. Age produced a small difference

00:06:33.020 --> 00:06:38.780
with younger participants showing the pattern more consistently. The study measured turning behavior

00:06:38.780 --> 00:06:44.220
directly during natural movement. No external factors overrode the directional preference.

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:49.760
Most people assume their direction choices while walking a random or shaped mainly

00:06:49.760 --> 00:06:55.840
by culture inhabit. In reality, humans carry an inherent bias toward counterclockwise turns

00:06:55.840 --> 00:07:01.780
that appears across tested populations. Right now, as you navigate a hallway or sidewalk,

00:07:02.320 --> 00:07:07.400
that same directional preference is likely influencing which way you veer when space opens up.

00:07:08.140 --> 00:07:14.100
The studies found the pattern held in groups of different sizes and showed only a modest weakening

00:07:14.100 --> 00:07:20.620
with age. One memorable detail is that the vast majority of participants followed the counterclockwise

00:07:20.620 --> 00:07:27.140
rule, regardless of gender or background. The next time you observe crowd flow in a public space,

00:07:27.640 --> 00:07:31.100
notice whether the collective drift matches this built-in tendency.

00:07:31.920 --> 00:07:37.820
Researchers can now design clearer experiments on navigation aids or building layouts that either work

00:07:37.820 --> 00:07:45.000
with or against the bias. Neolithic burials revealed dozens of headless skeletons uncovered by archaeologists

00:07:45.000 --> 00:07:52.640
in southwestern Slovakia. The skeletons date to approximately 7,000 years ago. Evidence indicates

00:07:52.640 --> 00:07:58.620
deliberate burial after death. The pattern may reflect a specific neolithic mortuary practice.

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:05.880
Further analysis of the site continues. Development displaces millions of amphibians without follow-up

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:12.400
according to UBC researchers who documented more than five million amphibians and reptiles moved

00:08:12.400 --> 00:08:19.080
in British Columbia over four years. No legal requirement exists to track post-relocation survival.

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:25.540
The study is the first to quantify the scale of such relocations in the province. Data come from

00:08:25.540 --> 00:08:32.880
development permits. Long-term outcomes remain unknown. Before we go, keep an eye on further validation

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:39.520
work for the mammogram AI tool in larger cohorts. That's Planetarian Daily for Today. If you

